Goal includes candidate_prepared shift_candidate_beta (need to prepare).

Goal includes candidate_task_profile_linked shift_candidate_beta route_task_profile_alpha (we already have linked? Actually init has candidate_transport_vehicle_linked? Wait we have candidate_task_profile_linked? For shift_candidate_beta, we have candidate_transport_leg_linked but not candidate_task_profile_linked. Init only has candidate_task_profile_linked for shift_candidate_alpha. So we need to attach task profile to shift_candidate_beta.

Goal includes candidate_clearance_established shift_candidate_beta (need to establish clearance). That requires loading verified, compliance certificate linked, etc.

Goal includes compliance_validation_complete shift_candidate_alpha (need to achieve for alpha). Also constraint_applied shift_candidate_alpha (need to apply operational constraint). Also operator_alignment_confirmed shift_candidate_alpha.

Goal includes candidate_finalized shift_candidate_alpha (need to finalize). There are multiple ways to finalize: finalize_candidate_direct, finalize_candidate_after_sequence_validation, finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation. Since we need compliance_validation_complete shift_candidate_alpha, we could use finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation.

Goal includes candidate_dispatch_slot_linked for each of the three candidates to dispatch_slot_alpha. So we need to allocate dispatch slot to each. However dispatch_slot_alpha is a single object; can it be linked to multiple candidates? The action allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate has precondition dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot and effect not (dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot). So after first allocation, dispatch_slot_available becomes false, preventing further allocations. So we cannot allocate the same dispatch slot to multiple candidates unless we release it. There's no release dispatch slot action. However after dispatch (execute_*_dispatch), the effect includes dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot (makes it available again). So we can allocate, dispatch, then allocate again to another candidate.

Thus we need to allocate dispatch slot to origin_availability_alpha, dispatch it (making slot available again), allocate to destination_availability_alpha, dispatch, allocate to shift_candidate_alpha, dispatch. Or any order.

